# Q: where do the three bases stand now, and on what ground?
#
# The bases are asked for hardcoded positions and the terrain comes from the seed, so
# whether a faction's headquarters lands on land is luck. On the standard seed the luck
# ran out: the Soviet base and its power plant, factory and design bureau all stood in
# deep water, with the starting force shoved onto the nearest shore and the base itself
# unreachable for the whole match. The scenario now searches for a patch of ground with
# room for a base, and this is where the search leaves the three of them.

units soviet 8
units chinese 1
units western 1
unit 0

# The ground under each headquarters, one cell at a time: the surface, the height against
# the water line, and what every movement class pays to stand on it. A base cell that says
# "deepwater impassable" is the bug; a forest a tank crosses at 280 per mille is a base a
# tank can drive to.
attributes -248.4 -117.2
attributes 145.3 -98.5
attributes -4.7 192.1

# The cell a Soviet tank starts on, taken from the formation in the units list above: the
# starting force stands around its base, on ground its own movement class can occupy.
attributes -215.4 -98.5

# And the map as a whole, because a base on land is worth nothing if the land is an island.
surfaces

# The same answer as a picture: the Soviet base on its patch of ground, from 150 m up.
focus -248.4 -117.2
zoom 150
shot artifacts/probe/base-ground.png

# The numbers above are a ledger: these are the sites the search settles on for this seed,
# and the costs under them are what says the bases are usable at all — a cost of zero is
# water or lava, and a base standing in either is a base nobody can reach.
expect "the Soviet base is at x -248.4 m" -248.4 -248.4 0.1
expect "the Soviet base is at z -117.2 m" -117.2 -117.2 0.1
expect "the Chinese base is at x 145.3 m" 145.3 145.3 0.1
expect "the Western base is at z 192.1 m" 192.1 192.1 0.1
expect "foot pays 140 per mille on the Soviet base" 140 140
expect "tracks pay 280 per mille on the Soviet base" 280 280
expect "tracks pay 100 per mille on the Chinese base" 100 100
expect "the map has deep water on it still" 866 866
